# Pragmate UI Form Controls Guide

## Overview

This guide explains how to use all the form control components available in Pragmate UI for building forms. All
components follow the beyond.js architecture and use the `/*bundle*/` magic comment.

## Core Form Component

### Form Container

[form.tsx](mdc:src/modules/form/controls/ts/form.tsx) - The main form wrapper that handles form submission and prevents
default browser behavior.

**Usage:**

```tsx
<Form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>{/* form controls go here */}</Form>
```

**Features:**

-   Automatically prevents default form submission
-   Stops event propagation
-   Accepts all standard HTML form attributes
-   Provides `onSubmit` callback for custom handling

## Input Controls

### Input Component

[input/index.tsx](mdc:src/modules/form/controls/ts/input/index.tsx) - Versatile input component with multiple variants
and validation support.

**Variants:**

-   `unstyled` - Basic input without styling
-   `floating` - Material Design floating label style
-   Default - Standard styled input

**Features:**

-   Multiple input types (text, password, date, time, etc.)
-   Icon support with floating variant
-   Built-in error handling and display
-   Controlled and uncontrolled modes
-   Date input special handling
-   Pattern validation support

**Usage Examples:**

```tsx
// Basic input
<Input
  type="text"
  label="Username"
  required
  placeholder="Enter username"
/>

// Floating label with icon
<Input
  type="email"
  variant="floating"
  label="Email"
  icon="email"
/>

// With validation
<Input
  type="password"
  label="Password"
  hasError={true}
  errorMessage="Password is required"
/>

// Date input
<Input
  type="date"
  label="Birth Date"
/>
```

### Textarea Component

[textarea/index.tsx](mdc:src/modules/form/controls/ts/textarea/index.tsx) - Multi-line text input with auto-resize and
counter support.

**Features:**

-   Auto-resize functionality (can be disabled)
-   Character counter
-   Error handling
-   Multiple variants (unstyled, floating)
-   Required field indication

**Usage:**

```tsx
<Textarea label="Description" placeholder="Enter description" counter={true} maxLength={500} variant="floating" />
```

### Select Component

[select/index.tsx](mdc:src/modules/form/controls/ts/select/index.tsx) - Dropdown selection component.

**Features:**

-   Options array support
-   Custom option rendering
-   Label support
-   Unique ID generation

**Usage:**

```tsx
<Select
	label="Country"
	options={[
		{ value: 'us', label: 'United States' },
		{ value: 'ca', label: 'Canada' },
	]}
/>
```

## Checkable Controls

### Checkbox Component

[checkbox/index.tsx](mdc:src/modules/form/controls/ts/checkbox/index.tsx) - Checkbox input with custom styling.

**Features:**

-   Custom SVG checkmark
-   Label support
-   Disabled state
-   Click event handling

**Usage:**

```tsx
<Checkbox label="Accept terms" checked={accepted} onChange={handleChange} />
```

### Radio Component

[radio.tsx](mdc:src/modules/form/controls/ts/radio.tsx) - Radio button input.

**Features:**

-   Custom styling
-   Label support
-   Click event handling
-   Group support (use same name attribute)

**Usage:**

```tsx
<Radio
  name="gender"
  value="male"
  label="Male"
  onChange={handleChange}
/>
<Radio
  name="gender"
  value="female"
  label="Female"
  onChange={handleChange}
/>
```

### Switch Component

[switch.tsx](mdc:src/modules/form/controls/ts/switch.tsx) - Toggle switch component.

**Features:**

-   Multiple variants (primary, secondary, etc.)
-   Size options (xs, sm, md, lg, xl)
-   Custom styling
-   Controlled state

**Usage:**

```tsx
<Switch checked={enabled} onChange={handleToggle} variant="primary" sizing="md" />
```

## Form Building Patterns

### Basic Form Structure

```tsx
<Form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
	<Input type="text" label="Full Name" required variant="floating" />

	<Input type="email" label="Email" required variant="floating" />

	<Textarea label="Message" placeholder="Your message here" counter={true} />

	<Select label="Category" options={categories} />

	<div className="checkbox-group">
		<Checkbox label="Subscribe to newsletter" checked={subscribed} onChange={handleSubscribe} />
	</div>

	<Button type="submit" variant="primary">
		Submit
	</Button>
</Form>
```

### Validation Patterns

```tsx
// Client-side validation
<Input
  type="email"
  label="Email"
  hasError={!isValidEmail}
  errorMessage={emailError}
  pattern="[a-z0-9._%+-]+@[a-z0-9.-]+\.[a-z]{2,}$"
/>

// Controlled validation
<Input
  type="password"
  label="Password"
  hasError={passwordError}
  errorMessage={passwordErrorMessage}
  value={password}
  onChange={handlePasswordChange}
/>
```

### Form State Management

```tsx
const [formData, setFormData] = useState({
	name: '',
	email: '',
	message: '',
	category: '',
	subscribed: false,
});

const handleInputChange = (field, value) => {
	setFormData(prev => ({
		...prev,
		[field]: value,
	}));
};

const handleSubmit = event => {
	event.preventDefault();
	// Process form data
	console.log(formData);
};
```

## Best Practices

1. **Use appropriate variants** for your design system
2. **Implement proper validation** with error states
3. **Group related controls** logically
4. **Use consistent labeling** across all form controls
5. **Handle form submission** properly with the Form component
6. **Provide clear error messages** for validation failures
7. **Use controlled components** when you need form state management
8. **Implement accessibility features** like proper labels and ARIA attributes

## Component Dependencies

All form controls extend from the base Pragmate UI interfaces:

-   [types/index.ts](mdc:src/modules/form/controls/ts/types/index.ts) - Common form interfaces
-   `IPUIProps` from `pragmate-ui/base` - Base component properties
-   Context providers for complex input components

## Styling

Form controls use SCSS modules located in [scss/](mdc:src/modules/form/controls/scss/) directory. Each component has its
own stylesheet for customization. description: globs: alwaysApply: false

